Changes from the written program (Nov 16 2026):
- Week 1 Saturday deadlift back-offs read 77.5% of that day''s single (≈ 70–72.5% of a Training Max) instead of % TM: there is no conventional Training Max yet (Jared switched back from sumo on Nov 7), so the single is the calibration and nothing is invented.
- Week 1 Tuesday paused deadlift is RPE-only for the same reason; from Week 2 it''s ~60% of the deadlift TM once the coach sets it.
- High Bar Squat and 2ct Paused Bench carry a % of the competition Training Max (High Bar 65–72.5%, 2ct bench 67.5–80%) with the written RPE as the cap: matched to his own recent sets (High Bar 165.6 kg × 6 @4 on Nov 12, 2ct bench 106.6 kg × 6 @5 on Nov 13), per the hybrid system''s ''percentage where reliable''.
- An optional 10-min Zone 2 on Thursday in Weeks 1–3 and 5–7 so cardio reaches the stated ~2 exposures a week (Weeks 2–7 only listed Tuesday).
- Primary bench uses the canonical Competition Bench (his Oct–Nov top sets were logged as Paused Bench Press).
- Week 9 Tuesday has no paused deadlift row (the default is none; add one only for a technical reason).
- Week 12 Tuesday is an optional session, and every Week 11–12 day is locked to its meet-relative date so an automatic re-plan can never slide the taper.' ELSE coach_notes END
   WHERE id = c_prep;
  UPDATE public.pl_blocks b SET name = r.to_name, sort_order = r.ord
    FROM jn_renames r WHERE b.id = r.id AND b.prep_id = c_prep AND b.name = r.from_name;
  GET DIAGNOSTICS v_n = ROW_COUNT;
  IF v_n <> 4 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'jared nationals corrections: renamed % blocks, expected 4', v_n; END IF;

  -- ── 3. the taper's wording ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  -- Week 11 and Week 12 wording (only where it's still exactly as written on Nov 16)
  UPDATE public.pl_weeks w SET notes = 'Week 11 of 12. The final meaningful heavy exposure for each lift: squat Monday, bench Thursday, deadlift Saturday. For now they''re counted from Feb 8, the conservative anchor (~14, ~11 and ~9 days out), and those are placeholders: once the lifting day is confirmed, each lift''s last heavy day is set on its own from Jared''s past meets and how he''s recovering this prep, so they may move apart or closer. Don''t max out.'
   WHERE w.block_id = '887f6705-82a0-45e7-92d6-0ab770c91318' AND w.week_index = 3 AND w.notes = 'Week 11 of 12. Final meaningful heavy exposures, counted from Feb 8 (the conservative meet anchor): squat Monday (~14 days out), bench Thursday (~11), deadlift Saturday (~9). Don''t max out. These dates move with the actual lifting day once it''s confirmed.';
  UPDATE public.pl_weeks w SET notes = 'Week 12 of 12. Taper, anchored on Feb 8 (the earliest day of the Feb 8–13 window). Once the lifting day is confirmed these sessions move with it: the primer stays two days out and the light technique work stays at least two days after each lift''s final heavy day. Weeks 1–10 stay as they are.'
   WHERE w.block_id = 'f4a16ece-9988-4ed5-8cec-0a44943f05ae' AND w.week_index = 1 AND w.notes = 'Week 12 of 12. Taper, anchored on Feb 8 (the earliest day of the Feb 8–13 window). Once the exact lifting day is confirmed these sessions move with it, keeping their distance from the meet; Weeks 1–10 stay as they are.';
  UPDATE public.pl_roadmap_notes n SET coach_summary = 'The last meaningful heavy single for each lift, strong and clean, never a grinder. For now ~14 / ~11 / ~9 days before Feb 8 (squat / bench / deadlift); each lift gets its own timing once the lifting day is confirmed.', edited_at = now()
    FROM public.pl_weeks w
   WHERE n.week_id = w.id AND w.block_id = '887f6705-82a0-45e7-92d6-0ab770c91318' AND w.week_index = 3
     AND n.coach_summary = 'The last meaningful heavy single for each lift: squat ~14 days out, bench ~11, deadlift ~9 (from Feb 8). Strong and clean, never a grinder.';
  UPDATE public.pl_blocks SET goal = 'Specificity: competition lifts only, heavy doubles and singles, then each lift''s final heavy exposure (placeholders ~14 / 11 / 9 days before Feb 8 until the lifting day is confirmed).' WHERE id = '887f6705-82a0-45e7-92d6-0ab770c91318' AND goal = 'Specificity: competition lifts only, heavy doubles and singles, then the final heavy exposures ~14 / 11 / 9 days out.';
  UPDATE public.pl_blocks SET coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Weeks 9–11 (Jan 10 – Jan 30). Week 11''s sessions are counted back from Feb 8 and locked to their dates. When the lifting day is confirmed, Confirm lifting day (Jared''s Training tab) plans each lift''s final heavy day from his past meets and this prep''s response, or keeps the even shift; nothing in Weeks 1–10 moves.' WHERE id = '887f6705-82a0-45e7-92d6-0ab770c91318' AND coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Weeks 9–11 (Jan 10 – Jan 30). Week 11''s sessions are counted back from Feb 8 and locked to their dates; when the lifting day is confirmed run pl_prep_set_meet_day to move them with it.';
  UPDATE public.pl_blocks SET coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Week 12 (Jan 31 – Feb 6), anchored on Feb 8. Locked to meet-relative dates; moves with the confirmed lifting day (Confirm lifting day on the Training tab). Keep a bench exposure close to the meet: Jared responds well to it.' WHERE id = 'f4a16ece-9988-4ed5-8cec-0a44943f05ae' AND coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Week 12 (Jan 31 – Feb 6), anchored on Feb 8. Locked to meet-relative dates; moves with the confirmed lifting day (pl_prep_set_meet_day). Keep a bench exposure close to the meet: Jared responds well to it.';
  UPDATE public.pl_blocks SET coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Weeks 1–4 (Nov 15 – Dec 12). Squat TM 235 kg / bench TM 150 kg (Sep 20 2026 meet; Nov 9 squat 192.8 × 4 @6 ≈ 245 e1RM, Nov 12 bench 115.7 × 4 @6 ≈ 147). Bench is watched from the first sessions: if % work runs past its RPE caps in 2+ sessions, the Training tab flags it with a slightly lower TM (never from one session). Conventional deadlift TM: not on file (never the 270 kg sumo meet pull); after Saturday Nov 21''s single @6 and back-offs the Training tab suggests a conservative one (92.5% of the estimated max) for you to set. Review all three after Week 4.' WHERE id = '3f736c8c-f785-4114-b3c5-d76f1af87a50' AND coach_notes = 'Nationals prep Weeks 1–4 (Nov 15 – Dec 12). Squat TM 235 kg / bench TM 150 kg (Sep 20 2026 meet; Nov 9 squat 192.8 × 4 @6 ≈ 245 e1RM, Nov 12 bench 115.7 × 4 @6 ≈ 147). Conventional deadlift TM: not on file; Jared switched back from sumo Nov 7 and his only conventional set since is 224.5 kg × 4 @10 (Nov 13, ≈ 252 e1RM). Set it after Saturday Nov 21''s single @6 (about 95% of that single''s e1RM, floored to 2.5 kg). Review all three after Week 4.';

  -- ── 4. the library template mirrors the 12 weeks ─────────────────────────
  UPDATE public.pl_templates t
     SET weeks = 12,
         tags = ARRAY['12 Weeks', '4 Days/Week', 'Powerlifting', 'Meet Prep', 'Hybrid % + RPE']::text[],
         description = 'The 12-week 2027 Nationals prep: Base, Strength, Peak, Taper. 4 days a week (Mon/Tue/Thu/Sat).',
         notes = 'Weekly order: MON Primary Squat + Bench/Triceps Overload; TUE Low-Fatigue Development + optional paused conventional pull; WED rest; THU Secondary Squat + Primary Competition Bench; FRI rest; SAT Primary Competition Deadlift + Secondary Bench; SUN rest.

The 12-week 2027 Nationals prep: Base (W1–4, W4 fatigue reduction), Strength (W5–8, W8 fatigue reduction), Peak (W9–11), Taper (W12). The off-season Jared trained before it (Sep 27 – Nov 14 2026) is its own program.

Loading: top singles by RPE; back-offs and competition-related secondaries as a % of the Training Max with the RPE as the cap (the cap beats the %); accessories by RPE with double progression, 1 hard set (2 for lats, side and rear delts).

Optional exercises are marked optional (Tuesday''s paused conventional pull, optional back-offs, accessories and cardio): skipping one never counts against him. Keep the paused pull only while Saturday''s deadlift keeps progressing.

Taper (Weeks 11–12): the final heavy squat / bench / deadlift days are placeholders counted from Feb 8 (~14 / ~11 / ~9 days out). Once the lifting day is confirmed, plan each lift on its own: bench recovers fastest and can sit closest (5–11 days out), squat 8–14, deadlift 8–16 and the lift most likely to need the most room. Read his own meets: Aug 5 2026 (NAPF), all three final heavies 10 days out, his best-peaked meet; Sep 20, near-max singles 7 days out, squat and bench peaked lower (he pulled sumo then, conventional now, so the deadlift evidence is weaker). Read this prep too: a lift whose % work keeps running past its RPE caps needs more room. Keep heavy days 2+ days apart (squat and deadlift 3+), light technique work 2+ days after that lift''s final heavy, the primer 2 days out, and never rewrite Weeks 1–10 for the taper.

Training Maxes: squat 235 / bench 150 kg, block-scoped and held. Change one only from a trend (2+ sessions past their RPE caps at the planned loads, never one), slightly (5% at most at once), and the coach sets it. Conventional deadlift: none until the Week 1 calibration (Sat Nov 21), then a conservative one from that single and its back-offs, set by the coach, never from the 270 kg sumo meet pull.

Changes from the written program, and why:
- Week 1 Saturday deadlift back-offs read 77.5% of that day''s single (≈ 70–72.5% of a Training Max) instead of % TM: there is no conventional Training Max yet (Jared switched back from sumo on Nov 7), so the single is the calibration and nothing is invented.
- Week 1 Tuesday paused deadlift is RPE-only for the same reason; from Week 2 it''s ~60% of the deadlift TM once the coach sets it.
- High Bar Squat and 2ct Paused Bench carry a % of the competition Training Max (High Bar 65–72.5%, 2ct bench 67.5–80%) with the written RPE as the cap: matched to his own recent sets (High Bar 165.6 kg × 6 @4 on Nov 12, 2ct bench 106.6 kg × 6 @5 on Nov 13), per the hybrid system''s ''percentage where reliable''.
- An optional 10-min Zone 2 on Thursday in Weeks 1–3 and 5–7 so cardio reaches the stated ~2 exposures a week (Weeks 2–7 only listed Tuesday).
- Primary bench uses the canonical Competition Bench (his Oct–Nov top sets were logged as Paused Bench Press).
- Week 9 Tuesday has no paused deadlift row (the default is none; add one only for a technical reason).
- Week 12 Tuesday is an optional session, and every Week 11–12 day is locked to its meet-relative date so an automatic re-plan can never slide the taper.',
         payload = jsonb_set(t.payload, '{blocks}', (
           SELECT jsonb_agg(
                    jsonb_set(jsonb_set(jsonb_set(b, '{name}', to_jsonb(r.to_name)), '{order_index}', to_jsonb(r.ord)), '{weeks}', coalesce((
                      SELECT jsonb_agg(
                               jsonb_set(
                                 CASE WHEN w ->> 'notes' = 'Week 11 of 12. Final meaningful heavy exposures, counted from Feb 8 (the conservative meet anchor): squat Monday (~14 days out), bench Thursday (~11), deadlift Saturday (~9). Don''t max out. These dates move with the actual lifting day once it''s confirmed.' THEN jsonb_set(w, '{notes}', to_jsonb('Week 11 of 12. The final meaningful heavy exposure for each lift: squat Monday, bench Thursday, deadlift Saturday. For now they''re counted from Feb 8, the conservative anchor (~14, ~11 and ~9 days out), and those are placeholders: once the lifting day is confirmed, each lift''s last heavy day is set on its own from Jared''s past meets and how he''s recovering this prep, so they may move apart or closer. Don''t max out.'::text))
                                      WHEN w ->> 'notes' = 'Week 12 of 12. Taper, anchored on Feb 8 (the earliest day of the Feb 8–13 window). Once the exact lifting day is confirmed these sessions move with it, keeping their distance from the meet; Weeks 1–10 stay as they are.' THEN jsonb_set(w, '{notes}', to_jsonb('Week 12 of 12. Taper, anchored on Feb 8 (the earliest day of the Feb 8–13 window). Once the lifting day is confirmed these sessions move with it: the primer stays two days out and the light technique work stays at least two days after each lift''s final heavy day. Weeks 1–10 stay as they are.'::text))
                                      ELSE w END,
                                 '{days}', coalesce((
                                   SELECT jsonb_agg(jsonb_set(d, '{rows}', coalesce((
                                            SELECT jsonb_agg(CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM jn_optional o WHERE o.key = r.key AND o.week_no = word AND o.day_index = (d ->> 'day_index')::int AND o.sort_order = xo - 1)
                                                                 THEN x || '{"is_optional": true}'::jsonb ELSE x END ORDER BY xo)
                                              FROM jsonb_array_elements(d -> 'rows') WITH ORDINALITY AS xr(x, xo)), '[]'::jsonb)) ORDER BY dord)
                                     FROM jsonb_array_elements(w -> 'days') WITH ORDINALITY AS dr(d, dord)), '[]'::jsonb))
                               ORDER BY word)
                        FROM jsonb_array_elements(b -> 'weeks') WITH ORDINALITY AS wr(w, word)), '[]'::jsonb))
                    ORDER BY r.ord)
             FROM jsonb_array_elements(t.payload -> 'blocks') b
             JOIN jn_renames r ON r.key = b ->> 'key'))
   WHERE t.id = c_tpl;

  SELECT count(*) INTO v_n
    FROM public.pl_templates t, jsonb_array_elements(t.payload -> 'blocks') b, jsonb_array_elements(b -> 'weeks') w,
         jsonb_array_elements(w -> 'days') d, jsonb_array_elements(d -> 'rows') x
   WHERE t.id = c_tpl AND (x ->> 'is_optional')::boolean;
  IF v_n <> 29 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'jared nationals corrections: the template marks % optional rows, expected 29', v_n; END IF;

  INSERT INTO public.program_loading_update_backup (source_table, row_id, row_data)
  VALUES ('run', 'jared_nationals_corrections_2026_11_17', jsonb_build_object('optional_rows', 29, 'off_season_prep', c_off, 'applied_at', now()));
  RAISE NOTICE 'jared nationals corrections applied';
END
$jc$;
